          "old_start": 481,
          "old_end": 489,
          "new_start": 481,
          "new_end": 486,
          "old": "We shall use the following criterion of Xiao, a weak form of the\ntranscendental holomorphic Morse inequalities; it is the special case of\n\\cite[Theorem~1.4]{Xiao15}, stated there for hermitian metrics $\\omega$\nwith $\\partial\\bar\\partial\\omega^j=0$, in which the metric is K\\\"ahler.\nThe sharper criterion, with $4k$ replaced by $k$, was proved by\nPopovici \\cite[Theorem~1.1]{Pop16}, confirming a conjecture of\nBoucksom--Demailly--P\\u{a}un--Peternell in the K\\\"ahler case; the weak\nform suffices for our purposes.\n",
          "new": "We use Popovici's bigness criterion \\cite[Theorem~1.1]{Pop16},\nwhich improves the coefficient $4k$ in Xiao's criterion \\cite{Xiao15}\nto $k$. We prove the K\\\"ahler case needed here. The proof combines\nGauduchon duality, the smooth Monge--Amp\\`ere equation and\nCauchy--Schwarz.\n"
        },
        {
          "old_start": 493,
          "old_end": 494,
          "new_start": 490,
          "new_end": 491,
          "old": "$A^k-4kA^{k-1}\\cdot B>0$, then $A-B$ is big.\n",
          "new": "$A^k-kA^{k-1}\\cdot B>0$, then $A-B$ is big.\n"
        },
        {
